\cf0 Mulder, A. (1996). "Getting a grip on alternate controllers: Addressing the variability of gestural expression in musical instrument design."\
\pard\pardeftab720\li720\fi-720\ri-340\partightenfactor0
\cf0 	A new approach to instrument design focuses on the needs and preferences of individual performers, whose capacity for gestural expression and movement capabilities vary. In optimizing performer-instrument compatibility, representation plays an important role. Considering the use of the hand in musical performance, analysis distinguishes two basic types of hand movement and leads to the definition of instruments that can be reconfigured to accommodate individual gestural preferences and capabilities. [Abstractor: author]\
